<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Agency on behaviorengineering.ai</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/tags/agency/</link><description>Recent content in Agency on behaviorengineering.ai</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 23 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://behaviorengineering.ai/tags/agency/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Predictability is exactly what you automate first</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-05-23-tshirt-predictability-automates-first/</link><pubDate>Sat, 23 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-05-23-tshirt-predictability-automates-first/</guid><description/></item><item><title>⚓ Neutrality is a risky ride</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/social-protocols/2026-05-19-be-the-captain-not-the-vessel/</link><pubDate>Tue, 19 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/social-protocols/2026-05-19-be-the-captain-not-the-vessel/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;When you decide not to take a side, what actually happens to your agency?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliberate neutrality works when you&amp;rsquo;re actively investigating or following fair process. But neutral-by-default under pressure? That&amp;rsquo;s &lt;strong&gt;drift&lt;/strong&gt;. And once you&amp;rsquo;re drifting, you&amp;rsquo;re easy to steer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you don&amp;rsquo;t take a stance, the &lt;strong&gt;system nudges you&lt;/strong&gt; into roles it rewards. Depending on what the moment requires, you drift into becoming a &lt;strong&gt;silent bystander&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;eager recruit&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;compliant enforcer&lt;/strong&gt;. Risk spikes when things are &lt;strong&gt;unclear&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;time is tight&lt;/strong&gt;, a &lt;strong&gt;boss is watching&lt;/strong&gt;, or your &lt;strong&gt;identity feels on the line&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>When the model feels threatened</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-05-16-smart-cover-your-ears/</link><pubDate>Sat, 16 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-05-16-smart-cover-your-ears/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Boundaries, now with growth</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-05-14-cow-w12/</link><pubDate>Thu, 14 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/cows/2026-05-14-cow-w12/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Not protection, an escape</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-05-04-tshirt-not-protection-escape/</link><pubDate>Mon, 04 May 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-05-04-tshirt-not-protection-escape/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Prepared, then advance</title><link>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-03-20-tshirt-prepared-advance/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Mar 2026 01:00:00 +1100</pubDate><guid>https://behaviorengineering.ai/cognitive-memetics/t-shirt-art/2026-03-20-tshirt-prepared-advance/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>